      </math>
    </region>
    <region left="387" top="1728" width="392" height="96" color="#000000">
      <picture>
        <raw format="png" encoding="base64"></raw>
      </picture>
    </region>
    <region left="270" top="1818" width="499" height="147" color="#000000">
      <picture>
        <raw format="png" encoding="base64"></raw>
      </picture>
    </region>
    <region left="0" top="2007" width="773" height="23" color="#000000" bgColor="#ffff80" fontSize="10">
      <text lang="eng" width="773" fontFamily="Arial" fontSize="10">
        <content>
          <p style="background-color: #ffff80;">4. **Check if there's an input Vripple restriction. If not, assume a value lower than 5%.</p>
        </content>
      </text>
    </region>
    <region left="0" top="2034" width="238" height="29" color="#000000" fontSize="10">
      <math>
        <input>
          <e type="operand">Vrip.outmax</e>
          <e type="operand">0.05</e>
          <e type="operand">4.7</e>
          <e type="operator" args="2">*</e>
          <e type="operand" style="unit">V</e>
          <e type="operator" args="2">*</e>
          <e type="operator" args="2">:</e>
        </input>
        <contract>
          <e type="operand" style="unit">mV</e>
        </contract>
        <result action="numeric">
          <e type="operand">235</e>
        </result>
      </math>
    </region>
    <region left="0" top="2061" width="773" height="23" color="#000000" bgColor="#ffff80" fontSize="10">
      <text lang="eng" width="773" fontFamily="Arial" fontSize="10">
        <content>
          <p style="background-color: #ffff80;">5. **Analyze if the LDO's PSRR meets the requirements.</p>
        </content>
      </text>
    </region>
    <region left="0" top="2088" width="78" height="24" color="#000000" fontSize="10">
      <math optimize="2">
        <input>
          <e type="operand">PSRR</e>
          <e type="operand">39</e>
          <e type="operator" args="2">:</e>
        </input>
      </math>
    </region>
    <region left="108" top="2088" width="172" height="29" color="#000000" fontSize="10">
      <math>
        <input>
          <e type="operand">Vrip.in</e>
          <e type="operand">200</e>
          <e type="operand" style="unit">mV</e>
          <e type="operator" args="2">*</e>
          <e type="operator" args="2">:</e>
        </input>
        <result action="numeric">
          <e type="operand">0.2</e>
          <e type="operand" style="unit">V</e>
          <e type="operator" args="2">*</e>
        </result>
      </math>
    </region>
    <region left="306" top="2088" width="237" height="211" color="#000000">
      <picture>
        <raw format="png" encoding="base64"></raw>
      </picture>
    </region>
    <region left="0" top="2115" width="281" height="55" color="#000000" fontSize="10">
      <math>
        <input>
          <e type="operand">Vrip.out</e>
          <e type="operand">Vrip.in</e>
          <e type="operand">10</e>
          <e type="operand">PSRR</e>
          <e type="operand">20</e>
          <e type="operator" args="2">/</e>
          <e type="operator" args="1">-</e>
          <e type="operator" args="2">^</e>
          <e type="operator" args="2">*</e>
          <e type="operator" args="2">:</e>
        </input>
        <contract>
          <e type="operand" style="unit">mV</e>
        </contract>
        <result action="numeric">
          <e type="operand">2.244</e>
        </result>
      </math>
    </region>
    <region left="0" top="2304" width="780" height="53" color="#000000" fontSize="10">
      <text lang="eng" fontFamily="Arial" fontSize="10">
        <content>
          <p>The estimated output ripple at the 500 kHz switching frequency is 2.2 mVpp. NXP’s 50 mVpp limit applies from 1 MHz to 66 MHz. The datasheet provides typical PSRR data up to approximately 10 MHz, and the assignment does not specify the input ripple spectrum. Therefore, compliance across the full 1–66 MHz band cannot be verified from the available data.</p>
        </content>
      </text>
    </region>
    <region left="0" top="2358" width="773" height="38" color="#000000" bgColor="#ffff80" fontSize="10">
      <text lang="eng" width="773" fontFamily="Arial" fontSize="10">
        <content>
          <p style="background-color: #ffff80;">6. **Review the TJA1100 datasheet and check if there are startup and shutdown speed restrictions. If such restrictions exist, identify strategies to make it compatible with the LDO.</p>
        </content>
      </text>
    </region>
    <region left="0" top="2394" width="780" height="53" color="#000000" fontSize="10">
      <text lang="eng" fontFamily="Arial" fontSize="10">
        <content>
          <p>The TJA1100 tolerates slow and fast supply ramps and does not require a dedicated power sequence between VBAT and the 3.3 V supplies. NXP does not specify a numerical rise-time or fall-time limit for the supply rail. The host should allow 2 ms for PHY initialization after the supplies are available before accessing the management interface. </p>
        </content>
      </text>
    </region>
    <region left="0" top="2448" width="772" height="23" color="#000000" bgColor="#ffff80" fontSize="10">
      <text lang="eng" width="772" fontFamily="Arial" fontSize="10">
        <content>
          <p style="background-color: #ffff80;">7. **Analyze and review which input/output capacitors will be used according to the temperature range.</p>
        </content>
      </text>
    </region>
    <region left="0" top="2466" width="772" height="23" color="#000000" bgColor="#ffff80" fontSize="10">
      <text lang="eng" width="772" fontFamily="Arial" fontSize="10">
        <content>
          <p style="background-color: #ffff80;">8. **Determine if it's necessary to add noise reduction capacitors.</p>
        </content>
      </text>
    </region>
    <region left="0" top="2493" width="758" height="38" color="#000000" fontSize="10">
      <text lang="eng" fontFamily="Arial" fontSize="10">
        <content>
          <p>The datasheet defines the input and output capacitours as below. Also it states that there is no need for a separate noise filter capacitor.</p>
        </content>
      </text>
    </region>
    <region left="0" top="2529" width="737" height="169" color="#000000">
      <picture>
        <raw format="png" encoding="base64"></raw>
      </picture>
    </region>
